WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.500
08:00 — SIP tick. Salary day: Nida ticks the SIP on her phone so the line lives in the app, not in a buried email receipt.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:13.000
13:00 — Funds on iPad. Fund list on the iPad at lunch — NAVs visible, no lecture about what she “should” buy.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:19.500
19:00 — Monthly laptop. Month summary on the laptop replaces the spreadsheet she always meant to update on Sundays.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:26.000
19:40 — Watchlist trim. Watchlist trimmed on the laptop; fewer tickers, clearer intent, still zero advice.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:32.500
20:00 — Phone lock. Phone confirms the SIP line before she puts the device face-down. The SIP is a line, not a lecture.

